<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="021" project="visual-host-create-button-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Migrate CreateRecordWizard onto WizardFollowOns (delete duplicate)</title>
    <phase>D: WizardFollowOns Consolidation</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>3</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>020</dependencies>
    <blocks>030,040</blocks>
    <tags>shared-lib, consolidation, regression</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Migrates an existing orchestrator that Invoice/KPI wizards wrap</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Migrating the orchestrator that Event/Invoice/KPI wrap; regression-sensitive gate for B/C</model-tier-reason>
    <parallel-group>D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Migrate CreateRecordWizard to consume the shared WizardFollowOns module and delete its local FollowOnSteps/NextStepsStep + SendEmailStep copies. This orchestrator is wrapped by Event/Invoice/KPI wizards, so its follow-ons must come from the shared module.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer. Follow §11 (no duplicate follow-on impls).</role>
  <goal>CreateRecordWizard renders its Next Steps via WizardFollowOns (declaring its card set as FollowOnCardConfig[]); local FollowOnSteps.tsx + steps duplicates removed; no behavior change for existing wrappers (Matter/Project/Event).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §5.9. CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx is the richest existing copy — 020 generalized it. Its wrappers (CreateEventWizard, CreateProjectWizard) must keep working identically.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx (delete)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/steps/ (delete migrated ones)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/index.ts
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>Replace CreateRecordWizard's use of local NextStepsStep with WizardFollowOns FollowOnGrid + a FollowOnCardConfig[] declaring the current cards.</step>
    <step>Delete FollowOnSteps.tsx and the steps/ files that moved into WizardFollowOns; fix imports.</step>
    <step>Regression: exercise CreateEventWizard + CreateProjectWizard (which wrap CreateRecordWizard) — Next Steps cards + follow-on creation unchanged.</step>
    <step>Build + tests.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Bash (grep for removed symbols), Skill(code-review)</tools>
  <outputs>CreateRecordWizard on WizardFollowOns; duplicates deleted.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>No local NextStepsStep/SendEmailStep remains in CreateRecordWizard (grep clean).</criterion>
    <criterion>CreateEventWizard + CreateProjectWizard Next Steps behave identically (regression pass).</criterion>
    <criterion>Shared lib builds; tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <completion-notes date="2026-07-08" rigor="FULL" model-tier="opus">
    <summary>
      CreateRecordWizard now renders "Next Steps" via the shared WizardFollowOns FollowOnGrid,
      declaring its card set as a FollowOnCardConfig[] (assign-counsel / create-event / send-email).
      The selectedActions-diffing sync useEffect (~165 lines) was removed — FollowOnGrid drives
      addDynamicStep/removeDynamicStep imperatively at click time via the shell handle. A slim
      selection-watching effect retains the assign-work-defaults behavior (getAssignWorkDefaults
      applied once on first 'assign-counsel' selection). Follow-on step bodies now come from
      WizardFollowOns (AssignWorkFollowOnStep, CreateEventFollowOnStep, SendEmailFollowOnStep).
    </summary>

    <files-changed>
      <edited>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx</edited>
      <edited>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/index.ts (dropped exports of deleted files; removed IRecipientItem re-export to avoid root-barrel collision with WizardFollowOns)</edited>
      <edited>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/index.ts (flipped WizardFollowOns curated re-export block to plain `export * from './WizardFollowOns'` — the collision cause is gone)</edited>
      <deleted>CreateRecordWizard/FollowOnSteps.tsx</deleted>
      <deleted>CreateRecordWizard/steps/AssignWorkFollowOnStep.tsx</deleted>
      <deleted>CreateRecordWizard/steps/CreateEventFollowOnStep.tsx</deleted>
      <deleted>CreateRecordWizard/steps/DraftSummaryStep.tsx</deleted>
      <deleted>CreateRecordWizard/steps/RecipientField.tsx</deleted>
      <kept reason="not migrated — no WizardFollowOns successor">CreateRecordWizard/steps/AssignResourcesStep.tsx</kept>
      <kept reason="sibling CreateWorkAssignmentWizard (parallel task 023) still imports ../CreateRecordWizard/steps/SendEmailStep; that folder is task-023-owned and off-limits to task 021">CreateRecordWizard/steps/SendEmailStep.tsx</kept>
    </files-changed>

    <behavior-preservation>
      <item>Card ids unchanged (assign-counsel/create-event/send-email) → derived step ids (followon-*), canonical sidebar order, and IFinishContext.selectedActions values reaching wrappers are byte-identical.</item>
      <item>Sidebar step label for send-email kept as 'Send Email' (via stepLabel) even though the card reads 'Send Notification Email' — matches the old FOLLOW_ON_STEP_LABEL_MAP split exactly.</item>
      <item>Send Email canAdvance gate (To+Subject+Body all non-empty) preserved on the card config.</item>
      <item>Next Steps heading/subtitle/empty-hint text passed explicitly to FollowOnGrid to match the old NextStepsStep entityLabel-interpolated copy.</item>
      <item>Follow-on form state still owned by CreateRecordWizard refs; renderStep reads .current so state survives step navigation identically.</item>
    </behavior-preservation>

    <regression-findings>
      <wrapper name="CreateEventWizard">
        Interacts with CreateRecordWizard only via config/props (ICreateRecordWizardConfig, IFinishContext).
        Uses context.selectedActions.includes('send-email') + context.followOn.email*. Card id + gate preserved →
        behaves identically. Its task-015 associateToStep/initialAssociation/lockAssociation work lives entirely in
        CreateEventWizard.tsx + the CreateRecordWizard associate-step logic, NEITHER of which task 021 touched
        (CreateEventWizard.tsx not modified). Test CreateEventWizard.associateToStep passes.
      </wrapper>
      <wrapper name="CreateProjectWizard">
        Uses context.selectedActions.includes('assign-counsel'|'create-event'|'send-email') + context.followOn.* and
        getAssignWorkDefaults. All three card ids + the assign-work-defaults semantics preserved (defaults applied once on
        first selection via the new slim effect). projectService test passes. CreateProjectWizard.tsx not modified.
      </wrapper>
    </regression-findings>

    <shared-barrel-flip>
      Task 021 owns flipping the root components/index.ts WizardFollowOns block from the curated re-export to a plain
      `export * from './WizardFollowOns'`, because task 021 deleted the actual collision cause (CreateRecordWizard's
      duplicate exports of AssignWorkFollowOnStep / CreateEventFollowOnStep / WORK_ASSIGNMENT_PRIORITY /
      FOLLOW_ON_CANONICAL_ORDER / IRecipientItem + prop types). Removed the now-stale transitional comment. Also removed
      IRecipientItem from the CreateRecordWizard barrel to prevent a duplicate-export (TS2308) with WizardFollowOns at root.
      No CreateMatterWizard/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/SummarizeFilesWizard sections of that file were touched.
    </shared-barrel-flip>

    <deferral note="parallel-safety, path A per CLAUDE.md §6.5">
      POML step 2 says delete SendEmailStep. Kept CreateRecordWizard/steps/SendEmailStep.tsx because a sibling-owned file
      (CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/WorkAssignmentWizardDialog.tsx, parallel task 023) still imports it directly and that
      folder is off-limits to task 021. Deleting now would red-build a file task 021 cannot edit. SendEmailStep is fully
      migrated as WizardFollowOns/SendEmailFollowOnStep; its physical removal should follow task 023 migrating off the
      direct import. Barrel still exports SendEmailStep for that consumer. This is the single acceptance-criterion nuance:
      "no local SendEmailStep remains in CreateRecordWizard" is satisfied for CreateRecordWizard's OWN usage (it now uses
      SendEmailFollowOnStep) but the file itself remains for the cross-task consumer.
    </deferral>

    <verification>
      <build>npm run build (tsc) — PASS, 0 errors. Confirms CreateRecordWizard on WizardFollowOns + both barrel flips are collision-free and all wrappers (Event/Project/Todo/Matter/WorkAssignment/SummarizeFiles) typecheck.</build>
      <lint>eslint on the 3 edited files — clean (no errors; no unused vars / hook-dep issues).</lint>
      <tests>jest — affected suites: CreateRecordWizard/CreateEventWizard/CreateProjectWizard/CreateTodoWizard/WizardFollowOns = 9 suites / 58 tests PASS. Sibling suites CreateMatterWizard/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard = 2 suites / 11 tests PASS.</tests>
      <grep>No live references to NextStepsStep/FollowOnSteps/deleted step paths/FOLLOW_ON_STEP_*_MAP remain (only descriptive comments).</grep>
      <quality-gates>code-review: clean (ADR-012 context-agnostic prop-driven preserved; ADR-021 Fluent v9 semantic tokens, 0 hardcoded hex, 0 v8 imports, 0 any-types; net LOC roughly flat, complexity reduced by removing the diffing effect). adr-check: no violations (no BFF changes; ADR-012/021/011 compliant).</quality-gates>
    </verification>
  </completion-notes>
</task>
